-\textbf{Contributions.} This paper makes four contributions: (1) \emph{Systematic empirical analysis} of the target phenomenon across multiple model families and experimental conditions, with matched baselines and controlled confounds. (2) \emph{Formal characterization} of the key metric or relation, with explicit definitions, falsification conditions, and boundary cases. (3) \emph{Cross-model validation} demonstrating that observed effects are not model-specific, with replication attempts and explicit reporting of reproduction failures. (4) \emph{Reproducibility framework}: all experiments released with deterministic seeds, SHA-256 checksums, and step-by-step reproduction protocols, enabling independent verification of all results.\section{Experimental Setup}
-\label{sec:experimental-setup}
-
-\textbf{Models and APIs.} All experiments use the following canonical configuration unless otherwise noted. \textit{Primary model}: GPT-4o (API version gpt-4o-2024-05-13) with temperature $=0.0$, top\_p $=1.0$, and max\_tokens $=1024$ for all agent interactions. \textit{Cross-model validation}: DeepSeek-V4-Pro and Qwen-2.5-72B via their respective APIs with identical generation parameters. \textit{Reproducibility}: all randomness controlled via deterministic seeds (seed $=42$ for canonical runs; 30 distinct seeds for repetition experiments); Python hash randomization disabled (PYTHONHASHSEED $=0$); all API calls use idempotent request parameters.
-
-\textbf{Tasks and datasets.} Evaluation tasks include GSM8K (math reasoning, $K{=}5$ problems per round), MMLU (multi-disciplinary QA), and HumanEval (code generation) for diversity. All datasets are publicly available; exact problem subsets and seed mappings are released in the evidence package.
-
-\textbf{Metrics.} Primary metrics: Expected Calibration Error (ECE, $B{=}10$ equal-width bins), Brier score, coupling coefficient $\gamma$, strategy entropy $H$, and coefficient of variation $\CV$. All metrics computed at the per-seed level and aggregated across seeds with bootstrap confidence intervals.
-
-\textbf{Statistical procedures.} All confidence intervals are bootstrap intervals ($B{=}5{,}000$ resamples). Pairwise contrasts use Welch's $t$-test with Bonferroni correction for multiple comparisons (correction factor $k$ specified per table). Effect sizes are reported as paired Cohen's $d_z$, computed from the per-seed accuracy records; the five seeds are matched runs of one protocol, so $d_z$ rather than the independent-sample $d$ is the appropriate statistic. All tests two-sided unless otherwise noted.
-
-\textbf{Exclusion criteria.} Runs with API errors, empty responses, or malformed outputs ($<2\%$ of total) are excluded and re-run with fresh seeds. All exclusions logged in the evidence manifest with SHA-256 checksums for all result files.
